## Navigation Patterns

### Expo Router Usage
```typescript
import { useRouter } from 'expo-router';

const router = useRouter();

// Standard navigation
router.push('/communities');

// Tab navigation
router.push('/(tabs)/cbt');

// Modal presentation
router.push('/settings');

// Back navigation
router.back();

// Replace current screen
router.replace('/(tabs)');
```

### Navigation with Parameters
```typescript
// Navigate with params
router.push({
  pathname: '/thread/[id]',
  params: { id: threadId }
});

// Access params in component
import { useLocalSearchParams } from 'expo-router';

const { id } = useLocalSearchParams<{ id: string }>();
```

## Testing Guidelines

### Component Testing
```typescript
import { render, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react-native';
import { Card } from '@/components/Cards';

describe('Card', () => {
  it('renders correctly', () => {
    const { getByText } = render(
      <Card title="Test Title">Test Content</Card>
    );
    
    expect(getByText('Test Title')).toBeTruthy();
    expect(getByText('Test Content')).toBeTruthy();
  });

  it('handles press events', () => {
    const onPress = jest.fn();
    const { getByText } = render(
      <Card title="Test" onPress={onPress}>Content</Card>
    );
    
    fireEvent.press(getByText('Content'));
    expect(onPress).toHaveBeenCalled();
  });
});
```

### Hook Testing
```typescript
import { renderHook, waitFor } from '@testing-library/react-native';
import { useCurrentUser } from '@/hooks/useUser';

describe('useCurrentUser', () => {
  it('returns user data', async () => {
    const { result } = renderHook(() => useCurrentUser());
    
    await waitFor(() => {
      expect(result.current.data).toBeDefined();
    });
  });
});
```

## Mental Health Considerations

### UX Priorities
- Reduce friction for vulnerable users
- Clear, supportive messaging
- Crisis intervention handling
- Anonymous support emphasis

### Content Moderation
- Flag crisis-related content
- Implement reporting systems
- Maintain supportive community standards

### Accessibility
- Use semantic color contrast
- Provide clear error messages
- Support screen readers
- Test with different user abilities

## Code Quality

### ESLint Configuration
- Use Expo ESLint config
- Enable TypeScript strict mode
- Enforce consistent import order
- Require proper error handling

### Git Workflow
- Use conventional commits
- Create feature branches
- Reference issues in commits
- Test before merging

### Documentation
- Comment complex business logic
- Document service methods with JSDoc
- Explain mental health considerations
- Keep README updated

